split,
merge,
damage,
and:
false shift.

OUT-OF-BOX EXTENSION

The main architectural idea is:

TOPOLOGY
SHOULD HAVE
A DEVELOPMENTAL LIFECYCLE.

It can:

form,
mature,
be challenged,
split,
merge,
hibernate,
be damaged,
and:
regenerate.

But:

STRUCTURAL CHANGE
SHOULD ITSELF
BE EVIDENCE-BOUND.

This creates a possible hierarchy:

MEMBER EVIDENCE
->
BOUNDARY EVIDENCE
->
TOPOLOGY CANDIDATE
->
ACCEPTED TOPOLOGY
->
ACTION SCOPE.

No layer gains authority
merely because:
it is newer
or:
more active.

