PRIMARY ACCEPTANCE FINDING

The full stacked H143 schedule does NOT support:
bounded adaptive topology regeneration.

The adaptive policies fail to recover before later events accumulate.

Most importantly:

the topology-damage event causes:
a persistent structural collapse

that:
the frozen incremental candidate system does not repair.

The preregistered recovery metric also becomes:
UNINFORMATIVE

for damage and merge
because:
pre-event ARI has already fallen below the frozen 0.60 informativeness gate.

The split recovery metric is also weak in some worlds because:
the immediate split-induced ARI drop can be smaller than 0.05.

Therefore:

the structural-mutation rate,
windowed ARI,
quarantine trajectory,
and:
one-event controls

are required to interpret the primary run honestly.

