GENERAL PRINCIPLE

LOCAL STRUCTURAL ADAPTATION

and:

TOPOLOGY REGENERATION

ARE
DIFFERENT OPERATIONS.

Incremental split/merge/reassign repair is useful when:

MOST OF
THE ACCEPTED TOPOLOGY
IS STILL TRUSTWORTHY.

It can repair:
persistent split
and:
persistent merge.

But after:
broad membership corruption,

the accepted topology becomes:
a bad prior.

At that point:

MORE
LOCAL PATCHING

can become:
STRUCTURAL ANCHORING.

The organism needs a second mode:

RE-DEVELOP
TOPOLOGY
FROM
RELATIONAL EVIDENCE.

DECISION

AR-H143 is:

MIXED-NEGATIVE.

POSITIVE FOR

